.TH FREE 1
.UC
.SH NAME
free \- display memory usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
[
.B \-h
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Free
prints a compact memory summary from kernel
.IR sysctl (2)
data.
The default output is in kilobytes.
The
.B Mem
line reports pages managed by the VM allocator.  Reserved and bad physical
pages are excluded from
.BR total ;
.B used
includes active, inactive, wired, device-owned, and other allocator-owned
pages;
.B free
is the current allocatable page count; and
.B act
is the resident VM object subset.  Consequently, wired allocations such as a
dynamic framebuffer reduce the reported free memory.
The swap line reports the logical swap size visible to the kernel swap
allocator.  On systems with compressed RAM swap, this can be larger than the
raw backing store.
The
.B Phys
line reports all detected physical memory, including reserved pages.
.PP
The
.B \-h
option keeps the same units but uses a shorter display for small consoles.
.SH SEE ALSO
top(1), vmstat(1)
